{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"3775917a-833d-4552-a194-252df8dc722d","cycle":1,"digest":"24d2d12c60813b51563310e68f666f64e4bfc2bab7600bdca792306f78f6f874","engine_id":"claudeloop","event_id":"30bba220-8a4d-4cc6-aa7b-b1edd1db7599","job_id":"4c2ec03f-d670-44f9-9f05-47597984ab20","kind":"QuestionAsked","payload":{"blocking":false,"cycle":1,"default":"The feature works as intended, all tests pass, and documentation is updated","item_id":"success_criteria","stage":"context_free","text":"How will you know this is complete and successful?"},"phase":"design","produced_at":"2026-08-22T02:54:24.007754+00:00","project_id":"5ea01f61-8536-4ace-90cb-18700a12e410","provenance":"agent","seq":4}
{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"03bae509-3dc7-4b43-8b63-17e2d636bc2a","cycle":1,"digest":"f96fc9cf753990e90fc0deed0eab8509cf45da20c805622ca1aa84a4fe678dc7","engine_id":"claudeloop","event_id":"e3791bfe-0778-4009-97c2-b2e73919eb92","job_id":"4c2ec03f-d670-44f9-9f05-47597984ab20","kind":"AnswerGiven","payload":{"answer":"One PR. Two changes plus their failure semantics. (1) Check engines concurrently. (2) Stop rebuilding the world per engine: doctor opens build_app() three times in one invocation, and once MORE per engine when --record is passed. build_app creates an asyncpg pool AND applies migrations -- discovering 11 files, hashing each, querying schema_migration -- so a four-engine `doctor --conformance --record` runs the migration machinery five times to write four rows.","item_id":"scope"},"phase":"design","produced_at":"2026-08-22T02:59:00.626706+00:00","project_id":"5ea01f61-8536-4ace-90cb-18700a12e410","provenance":"trusted","seq":5}
{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"7ccb5530-620e-4a12-9ed2-5ec58558c454","cycle":1,"digest":"34a7f5a376f057ac6c44e6137eb0c717dbec790dcaf6376b673d1962197aba9a","engine_id":"claudeloop","event_id":"529108f0-903f-4807-a85f-44495cd16148","job_id":"4c2ec03f-d670-44f9-9f05-47597984ab20","kind":"AnswerGiven","payload":{"answer":"Make `vibey doctor` fast. Measured on this machine: 6.26s user CPU, 1.52s system, 11% CPU, 1:06.81 wall. Roughly 90% of that minute is spent waiting, not computing. The cause is structural -- doctor iterates engines in a plain `for desc in descriptors:` loop and awaits each engine's preflight subprocess in turn. Four independent engines that share no state are checked strictly one after another. `--conformance` is far worse, since each engine then spawns a real session; that is where cursorloop hung earlier and never returned.","item_id":"objective"},"phase":"design","produced_at":"2026-08-22T02:59:00.626706+00:00","project_id":"5ea01f61-8536-4ace-90cb-18700a12e410","provenance":"trusted","seq":6}
{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"e7f3c53d-646c-4fcf-8c16-91552c6e3747","cycle":1,"digest":"ebed982737c6d75ea0824e629fb21411c0ace02d4f42ee375f639372167005a8","engine_id":"claudeloop","event_id":"75c91168-e064-400c-8661-2911f23f403a","job_id":"4c2ec03f-d670-44f9-9f05-47597984ab20","kind":"AnswerGiven","payload":{"answer":"[hard] Concurrency changes failure semantics, and that is the actual work rather than the asyncio.gather. Today a hanging engine blocks everything visibly and in order; concurrently, one hung engine among four must not silently reduce the report to three. Per-engine timeout, and partial results that SAY they are partial. [hard] Output must stay deterministic -- engines reported in a stable order regardless of completion order, or the command becomes untestable and diffs become noise. [hard] One engine failing must not fail the others. [hard] Do not weaken any check to make it fast; correctness of the verdict is the point of the command. [hard] 100% branch coverage including the timeout and partial-result paths. [hard] Conventional Commits, feature branch into develop.","item_id":"constraints"},"phase":"design","produced_at":"2026-08-22T02:59:00.626706+00:00","project_id":"5ea01f61-8536-4ace-90cb-18700a12e410","provenance":"trusted","seq":7}
{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"08773c17-91df-4c6b-97cd-e1fe4874d523","cycle":1,"digest":"7f703cd3daa86539e6b597f007e670db9ee39aa133953024f70541b19c1900b9","engine_id":"claudeloop","event_id":"48a1151d-6a8b-4436-a6f5-c97095fbe180","job_id":"4c2ec03f-d670-44f9-9f05-47597984ab20","kind":"AnswerGiven","payload":{"answer":"Wall-clock for `vibey doctor` approaches the slowest single engine rather than the sum -- roughly 4x on this machine. Before/after numbers committed as evidence. A hung engine yields a report naming it as timed out while the other three report normally. All 7 gates green.","item_id":"success_criteria"},"phase":"design","produced_at":"2026-08-22T02:59:00.626706+00:00","project_id":"5ea01f61-8536-4ace-90cb-18700a12e410","provenance":"trusted","seq":8}
